\title{Bulk integers and boundary modes}
\date{2026-11-27}

\p{A Wilson mass separates the corners of the [momentum grid](fdip-013X) into two sets. Their orientations can be read before a link field is chosen. Which information about a charged field survives this count, and what can a boundary detect?}

